          %h2#history History
          %h3#very_early_sources_and_schools Very early sources and schools
          %p
            There are many sources of noncommutative spaces, e.g.
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            (Snyder studied an interesting noncommutative space in the late 1940s). It has been often noticed, since Gel’fand–Neimark’s work (see
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gelfand+spectrum"} Gelfand spectrum
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Banach+algebra"} Banach algebra
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Irving+Segal"} Irving Segal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alain+Connes"} Alain Connes
            (
            %a{:href => "http://www.alainconnes.org/"}> web site
            ) brought about a whole revolution in mathematics using the framework of noncommutative geometry based on
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operator+algebra"} operator algebra
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theory
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+theory"} ring theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum+%28geometry%29"} spectra
            of noncommutative rings or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian categories
            (the spectrum of indecomposable injectives of Gabriel, the affine spectrum of P. M. Cohn and so on) and stronger results in special cases like P. I. rings (polynomial identities rings) by M. Artin, F. van Oystaeyen and others in the 1970s. Golan and van Oystaeyen took noncommutative localization seriously in the mid 1970s with very promising results;
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Rosenberg"} A. Rosenberg
            found in 1982 the so-called
            %span.newWikiWord
              left spectrum
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/left+spectrum"} ?
            of a noncommutative ring, straightforwardly later generalized to a spectrum of an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+algebraic+geometry"} noncommutative algebraic geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+categories"} derived categories
            of (quasi)coherent sheaves complemented that effort (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mikhail+Kapranov"}> Kapranov
            , Bondal, Orlov, …). Though the effort was rather disconnected (from ring-theoretic mainstream noncommutative algebraic geometry) at the beginning, it can be now more easily judged as closely related; this is also the time of birth of the influential school of noncommutative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+geometry"} projective geometry
            (Artin, Smith, Zhang, …).
          %p
            The quantization program and the study of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integrable+systems"} integrable systems
            brought about a number of interesting examples (in the early phase by G. Kac, Sklyanin, Fadeev, Drinfel’d, Woronowicz, Jimbo,
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yuri+Manin"} Manin
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+groups"} quantum groups
            which were studied in a number of formalisms from operator algebraic to algebro-geometric and purely categorical.
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} Actions
            are very important in noncommutative geometry, and are some of the main examples in Connes’ school like group(oid)
            = succeed "-algebras," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^*
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+noncommutative+algebraic+geometry"} equivariant noncommutative algebraic geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf%E2%80%93Galois+extension"} Hopf–Galois extension
            and entwining structure.
          %p
            Noncommutative formal geometry, concerned with objects like infinitesimal neighborhoods of subvariaties, power series in noncommutative variables and so on, has been appearing more sporadically than the operator algebraic and algebro-geometric frameworks. Among pioneering works, there are
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kontsevich"} Kontsevich
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kapranov%27s+noncommutative+geometry"} Kapranov's noncommutative geometry
            “based on commutator expansions”. Noncommutative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analytic+geometry"} analytic geometry
            is even now only vaguely outlined in existing works.
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alain+Connes"}> Alain Connes
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Noncommutative+Geometry"} Noncommutative Geometry
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.elsevier.com/books/noncommutative-geometry/connes/978-0-08-057175-1"} ISBN:9780080571751
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.alainconnes.org/docs/book94bigpdf.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jos%C3%A9+Gracia-Bondia"}> José Gracia-Bondia
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joseph+Varilly"} Joseph Varilly
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Elements of noncommutative geometry
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-1-4612-0005-5"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4612-0005-5
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://books.google.hr/books?id=2yJIwWbh1isC&lpg=PP1&ots=ex0Xfmh_UU&dq=Varilly%20noncommutative&hl=en&pg=PP1#v=onepage&q=Varilly%20noncommutative&f=false"} gBooks
          %p Exposition:
          %ul
            %li#Lupercio20
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ernesto+Lupercio"}> Ernesto Lupercio
              ,
              %em Non-commutative Geometry Indomitable
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2008.08529"}> arXiv:2008.08529
              )
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li#Connes95
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alain+Connes"}> Alain Connes
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Noncommutative geometry and reality
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.alainconnes.org/docs/reality.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alain+Connes"}> Alain Connes
                ,
                %em A walk in the non-commutative garden
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0601054"}> arXiv:math/0601054
                )
          %p
            With a view towards
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motives+in+physics"} motives in physics
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alain+Connes"}> Alain Connes
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matilde+Marcolli"} Matilde Marcolli
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Noncommutative+Geometry%2C+Quantum+Fields+and+Motives"} Noncommutative Geometry, Quantum Fields and Motives
          %div
            %h3#ReferencesNoncommutativeGeometryOfFQHE Quantum Hall effect via non-commutative geometry
            %p
              Discussion of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integer+quantum+Hall+effect"} integer quantum Hall effect
              via a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brillouin+torus"} Brillouin torus
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+geometry"} noncommutative geometry
              and using the Connes-Chern character:
            %ul
              %li#BvESB94
                J. Bellissard, A. van Elst, H. Schulz-Baldes:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The noncommutative geometry of the quantum Hall effect
                %strong 35
                5373 (1994) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/cond-mat/9411052"}> cond-mat/9411052
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://link.aip.org/link/doi/10.1063/1.530758"} doi:10.1063/1.530758
            %p
              Generalization of
              %a{:href => "#BvESB94"} BvESB94
              to the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fractional+quantum+Hall+effect"} fractional quantum Hall effect
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matilde+Marcolli"}> Matilde Marcolli
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Varghese+Mathai"} Varghese Mathai
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Towards the fractional quantum Hall effect: a noncommutative geometry perspective
                = succeed "," do
